# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
Subject: [PATCH] fbdev: mdss: expose the existing platform link as device

The downstream framebuffer is intentionally a virtual device for its runtime
PM implementation. Changing framebuffer_alloc's parent prevents its runtime
state from becoming active and makes fb_open fail with ENOSYS.

The driver already exports its actual platform device through an mdss_fb link.
Expose that same target through the standard device link, allowing current
Xorg fbdevhw to identify its non-PCI subsystem while retaining the downstream
runtime PM hierarchy.

--- a/drivers/video/msm/mdss/mdss_mdp_overlay.c
+++ b/drivers/video/msm/mdss/mdss_mdp_overlay.c
@@ -5423,6 +5423,11 @@
 	if (rc)
 		pr_warn("problem creating link to mdss_fb sysfs\n");
 
+	rc = sysfs_create_link_nowarn(&dev->kobj,
+			&mfd->pdev->dev.kobj, "device");
+	if (rc)
+		pr_warn("problem creating framebuffer device link\n");
+
 	if (mfd->panel_info->type == MIPI_VIDEO_PANEL) {
 		rc = sysfs_create_group(&dev->kobj,
 			&dynamic_fps_fs_attrs_group);
